WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:01.182
- Oh my God!

00:00:03.351 --> 00:00:05.634
Look at your face!

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:07.426
- [Voiceover] I love
playing on the arcade.

00:00:07.426 --> 00:00:08.926
(energetic music)

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:12.917
- So I'm gonna be putting
prosthetic acne on my face.

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:14.488
- We're gonna wear it for a day.

00:00:14.488 --> 00:00:15.505
A day, right?

00:00:15.505 --> 00:00:17.643
- Both my parents have really clear skin,

00:00:17.643 --> 00:00:19.003
and that was just passed on to me.

00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:20.325
I can't take credit for any of that.

00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:23.286
- I definitely had acne
for most of my teen years.

00:00:23.286 --> 00:00:25.109
I'm really nervous about
this honestly (laughs).

00:00:25.109 --> 00:00:26.850
- I'm ready to be educated.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.767
- My name is Doctor Alex Martin.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.321
For the past 30 years,

00:00:30.321 --> 00:00:33.863
I have seen various degrees
of hormonally-related acne.

00:00:33.863 --> 00:00:34.697
- Does this make you puberty

00:00:34.697 --> 00:00:36.267
if you're giving me the acne?

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:37.483
- Does it stash?

00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:38.317
- Mm hm.

00:00:38.317 --> 00:00:40.063
- It's every 13-year-old
boy's mortal enemy.

00:00:40.063 --> 00:00:41.792
- [Alex] Ranging from very minor outbreaks

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:44.126
to the most severe cystic acne.

00:00:44.126 --> 00:00:45.287
- [Voiceover] So you're
about to see yourself.

00:00:45.287 --> 00:00:46.120
- Yeah, okay.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.470
So I'm gonna take a look.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:48.770
Oh, whoa!

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.781
- Oh shit, dude, I have plans today.

00:00:51.781 --> 00:00:53.333
- I'm just like looking at myself

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:55.017
and wondering what people are gonna say.

00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:56.699
- Well, I posted a selfie on Instagram.

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.499
All the comments were just people

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:01.160
like trying to console me.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.376
- Well, my friends are mostly assholes, so

00:01:03.376 --> 00:01:05.398
(laughs) when I posted the picture,

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.032
there was a lot of guys
who I think have found me

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:09.365
attractive at some point in my life were,

00:01:09.365 --> 00:01:11.670
felt the need that it was the right time

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.447
to tell me how terrible I look.

00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:18.265
- Social anxiety seems to be
a result of dealing with acne.

00:01:18.265 --> 00:01:20.935
- Finding it very hard to
look people right in the face,

00:01:20.935 --> 00:01:23.617
- I'm kind of amazed at how many people

00:01:23.617 --> 00:01:26.218
took no issue with just staring at me.

00:01:26.218 --> 00:01:28.842
When people stared it felt like,

00:01:28.842 --> 00:01:29.944
indeed, you have zits.

00:01:29.944 --> 00:01:31.569
- The first interaction
we have with people

00:01:31.569 --> 00:01:32.823
is by looking at them.

00:01:32.823 --> 00:01:34.565
So people fall guilty of staring.

00:01:34.565 --> 00:01:37.340
I think what we learned here
is to have more empathy.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:40.997
- You cannot really replicate
exactly the experience

00:01:40.997 --> 00:01:42.344
of the acne patient.

00:01:42.344 --> 00:01:43.656
- I'm really bummed out right now.

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:45.676
I can only imagine how it feels to wake up

00:01:45.676 --> 00:01:49.682
to an acne breakout and
have to get through the day.

00:01:49.682 --> 00:01:51.679
- But psychologically,
I think you're gaining

00:01:51.679 --> 00:01:52.955
a lot of information.

00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:54.781
- I'm kind of frustrated with myself

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.031
because of how I very badly

00:01:58.297 --> 00:02:00.677
want to tell them that it's fake.

00:02:00.677 --> 00:02:02.917
- So my day has kind of turned around.

00:02:02.917 --> 00:02:05.100
I just didn't really give a
shit at the end of the day.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.282
But that was not brought
on by just myself.

00:02:07.282 --> 00:02:08.502
It was brought on by my friends.

00:02:08.502 --> 00:02:10.496
We're in Whole Foods,
I didn't want to come.

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:11.856
- I made her come out because

00:02:11.856 --> 00:02:13.504
she has nothing to be ashamed of.

00:02:13.504 --> 00:02:15.584
- In the beginning, I was
kind of emotional and sad,

00:02:15.584 --> 00:02:17.336
and then I realized, I'm hungry,

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:18.718
I want to hang out with my friends,

00:02:18.718 --> 00:02:19.681
I want to laugh.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.581
- I have never been so excited

00:02:21.581 --> 00:02:23.583
to finish with shooting a video.

00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:26.184
I felt super duper
self-conscious of the way I look.

00:02:26.184 --> 00:02:28.564
To anybody who is dealing with acne,

00:02:28.564 --> 00:02:29.979
you are so much stronger than me.

00:02:29.979 --> 00:02:32.476
I had acne for a day, and I
wanted to hide under a rock.

00:02:32.476 --> 00:02:33.764
- I'm sure it's very genetic.

00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:35.238
I'm sure you can go to a dermatologist,

00:02:35.238 --> 00:02:36.644
and it takes time.

00:02:36.644 --> 00:02:38.164
I think it's just important to just

00:02:38.164 --> 00:02:40.359
practice self-love in other ways.

00:02:40.359 --> 00:02:44.040
- It's really character
and the talent that counts,

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.363
not superficial beauty.

00:02:45.363 --> 00:02:48.624
- This experiment not
only made me appreciate

00:02:48.624 --> 00:02:50.877
and understand the insecurities of acne,

00:02:50.877 --> 00:02:54.616
but made me just like love
myself a little bit more.

00:02:54.616 --> 00:02:57.542
This whole thing has been
very helpful with that.

00:02:57.542 --> 00:02:59.736
- If I was a stranger and
I asked for your number,

00:02:59.736 --> 00:03:01.825
would you, what would you say?

00:03:01.825 --> 00:03:04.102
- I would give you half of my number.

00:03:04.102 --> 00:03:06.365
Let me see what your personality is like,

00:03:06.365 --> 00:03:09.419
and then I give you the other half.

00:03:09.419 --> 00:03:11.161
- I get three-and-a-half digits

00:03:11.161 --> 00:03:13.328
is what he just said. (laughs)

00:03:13.328 --> 00:03:14.161
- Basically.

